rep('Chapters/08_Control_Firmware/15_PWR_2_Port.tex','On the F410, UART transmit is assigned to PA9,','On the F410, the serial-data transmit output (UART TX) is assigned to PA9,')
rep('Chapters/08_Control_Firmware/15_PWR_2_Port.tex','That command was moved to PB13/TIM1\\_CH1N, with PA8/TIM1\\_CH1 as its complement.',r'The low-side carrier command was moved to output PB13, connected internally to TIM1\_CH1N, while the paired high-side command uses PA8/TIM1\_CH1. CH1 names a timer output channel; CH1N is its complementary partner. The enable signal moved to PA11, allowing PA10 to become the serial-data receive input (UART RX). Thus PA10 is an enable output on the G071, but a receive input on the F410.')
rep('Chapters/08_Control_Firmware/15_PWR_2_Port.tex','At a \\SI{100}{\\mega\\hertz} TIM1 clock, the code sets ARR',r'The timer registers are stored hardware settings: ARR sets the count limit, CCR1 the output compare threshold, and DTG the programmed dead interval. At a \SI{100}{\mega\hertz} TIM1 clock, the code sets ARR')
rep('Chapters/08_Control_Firmware/15_PWR_2_Port.tex','The F410 ADC uses the same free-running scan of primary voltage, secondary-bulk voltage, and primary current.','The F410 analog-to-digital converter uses the same free-running scan of primary voltage, secondary-bulk voltage, and primary current. Here, a scan means sampling each sensing input in sequence; an ADC channel is the selected input, while DMA stream/channel labels identify the route used to copy the result into memory.')
